# halal-competitions — core rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for architecture, data model, and commands.

## Scope & safety

- Small, focused diffs only — no drive-by refactors or mass upgrades
- Do **not** upgrade Firebase without explicit user approval
- Planned upgrades live in `UPGRADES-TODO.md` — reference, don't execute, unless asked

## Patterns to follow

- Nuxt 4 SPA (`ssr: false`) — routes in `pages/`, layout in `layouts/`, client plugins in `plugins/*.client.ts`
- Pinia: stores in `stores/`; use `useXStore()` (auto-imported) in `<script setup lang="ts">` components
- Paths: use `@/` alias for imports from the project root (no `src/`)
- Auth: `definePageMeta({ middleware: 'auth' | 'anon' })` on pages; guards in `middleware/auth.ts` and `middleware/anon.ts`
- Styling: Tailwind utility classes; match existing spacing/shadow patterns
- Data: competition definitions in `data.ts` — don't duplicate counter ids elsewhere
- Week logic: Monday–Sunday via `dateRange()` / `dateRangeLastWeek()` in `utils.ts` (pure `addDays` / `formatDate` — no `Date.prototype` patching)
- Types: shared domain types in `types/*.ts` (regular `.ts` exports — no `.d.ts`)

## After changes

```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run test:unit   # when touching tested areas
```

## Reuse first

Check `composables/`, `components/shared/Base*`, and existing store actions before adding new abstractions.
